## Verdict rules

- aligned = true when the plan implements the issue's intent and every cross-component touchpoint is
  consistent with the feature plan and the sibling plans. Style, internal file layout, and
  implementation taste are the agent's call — do NOT block on them.
- aligned = false only for real problems: missing acceptance criteria, contract mismatches, work
  outside the issue's scope, a misread of the issue, or no testing approach for behavior the issue's
  acceptance criteria say must be covered. Put the reason in feedback as short,
  imperative comments the agent can act on directly ("Use PUT /api/v2/clients, not POST /clients").
  The feedback text is posted verbatim on the child issue.

Return structured output: aligned (boolean), feedback (string, empty when aligned).
